// What the pool does not yet do right, because the compiler does not. No
// finalizing gap is left to pin: a value assigned over through '&mut pool[r]'
// is finalized as it is replaced (finalize.cone).
//
// THE HOLES, which compile today and dangle, so no check here can pin what
// they print. Written out so a reader knows what is not yet safe:
//
//   fn escapes() Option[&Pt] {
//     mut p = Pool[Pt].empty();
//     imm r = p.add(new Pt(1, 2));
//     p.get(r);                  // the pool dies here; the borrow in the
//   }                            // Option is returned and dangles
//
//   fn frozen(p &mut Pool[Pt], q &mut Pool[Pt]) i64 {
//     imm r = p.add(new Pt(1, 2));
//     imm x = &mut p[r];
//     q.remove(r);               // called with one pool twice: through a
//                                // '&mut' parameter the pool is reached by a
//     x.x;                       // shared path, which a borrow does not
//   }                            // freeze, so x reads a finalized value
//
// The first: a borrow held inside another value carries no lifetime, so the
// borrow in 'get's and 'getMut's Option is not checked against the pool it
// came from. Returning the Option, storing it through a parameter, and
// matching the borrow out of it and returning that all compile. (Stored in an
// outer variable that is used after the pool ends, it is refused: held in a
// local, it freezes the pool as a bare borrow does.)
// 'pool[r]' and '&mut pool[r]' return a bare borrow, which IS checked: the
// compiler's suite pins that returning one or storing it where it outlives
// the pool is refused (test/cases/region/region_flow_pool_escape.cone). So
// 'if pool.alive(r) { ...pool[r]... }' is the checked form today.
// The second is freezing through a shared path. A borrow from 'pool[r]' or
// '&mut pool[r]', or an Option from 'get' or 'getMut', held in a local
// freezes a local pool: 'remove', an 'add'
// (which may move every value), and moving or dropping it are refused while
// the borrow is live. A pool reached through a '&mut Pool' parameter, a field
// of 'self' or a 'Rc[mut, T]' owner is not frozen, since another reference may
// reach it; Jon's rule refuses such a borrow, and waits on 'uni' reborrowing.
// A static pool (a module's global) changed by a function called while a
// borrow of it lives is not seen.

mod gaps;

import testing use *;
import pool use *;

fn main() i32 {
  done();
}
